Theorem L-7: Canonicalization idempotent

  Preconditions:
    - canonicalize is the lattice canonicalization function per
      Annex E §AIMS (CN-1, CN-2, CN-3, CN-5, CN-6, CN-8 — CN-4
      and CN-7 are REMOVED per sec-2 historical notes)
    - L-7 (idempotence) per Annex E §AIMS.8 L-7
    - canonicalize loops over the active CN-N rules until fixed point,
      bounded at 3 rounds per sec-2 (current rules reach fixpoint in
      one pass; multi-round loop = defensive)

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState. canonicalize(canonicalize(s)) = canonicalize(s)

  Proof obligation:
    Each individual CN-N rule is idempotent — once applied, re-application
    leaves the state unchanged. The full canonicalize() is the iterated
    composition of CN-1, CN-2, CN-3, CN-5, CN-6, CN-8 until fixed point;
    idempotence of the composition follows from per-rule idempotence +
    the fixpoint guarantee (3-round bound is defensive but each rule
    is one-pass-stable on canonical input).

    Per-CN-rule idempotence:
      CN-1 (Dead <-> Absent bidirectional):
        first pass coalesces (Dead, Absent) and (Linear, Absent) etc.
        per the matrix in sec-2; once both dimensions agree, the
        rule's predicate is satisfied (Consumption = Dead iff
        Cardinality = Absent), so re-application is a no-op.
      CN-2 (Linear + Absent infeasible):
        subsumed by CN-1; one pass eliminates the combination.
      CN-3 (Shared blocks reuse — Shape forced to NonReusable):
        on first pass, Uniqueness = Shared sets Shape to NonReusable;
        re-application sees Shape already NonReusable, no change.
      CN-5 (Unique + Dead preserves reusable shape):
        a no-mutation rule that documents an invariant; re-application
        observes the same invariant.
      CN-6 (Wide-locality uniqueness ceiling):
        first pass demotes Unique to MaybeShared when Locality >=
        HeapEscaping; re-application sees Uniqueness already MaybeShared
        (or wider), no change.
      CN-8 (Borrowed locality ceiling):
        first pass clamps Borrowed + Locality > FunctionLocal down to
        FunctionLocal; re-application sees Locality already
        FunctionLocal (or narrower), no change.

    Per-rule pre-canonicalization + post-canonicalization enumeration:
      Total 7-dim carrier sizes: 2 * 4 * 3 * 3 * 5 * 5 * 8 = 14,400 states.
      Each CN rule operates on a small slice (2-3 dimensions); per-rule
      fired-or-not predicate is decidable per state. Per-rule
      verification enumerates the small slice (e.g. CN-1 covers
      Consumption x Cardinality = 4 * 3 = 12 pairs; CN-3 covers
      Uniqueness x Shape = 3 * 5 = 15 pairs; CN-6 covers
      Locality x Uniqueness = 5 * 3 = 15 pairs; CN-8 covers
      Access x Locality = 2 * 5 = 10 pairs).

    Composition idempotence:
      Apply the full canonicalize(s) to obtain s'. By per-rule
      idempotence, applying canonicalize(s') = s' (no rule fires
      again; all conditions are already in canonical form). Therefore
      canonicalize(canonicalize(s)) = canonicalize(s).

    Sentinel handling per L-9: SCALAR is pre-filtered before any
    canonicalize invocation; canonicalize does not propagate SCALAR.
    FRESH / CONSERVATIVE / ALL / NONE are concrete 7-tuples whose
    canonical forms equal themselves (verified by per-sentinel
    canonicalize invocation in the engine discharge).

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-CN-rule idempotence enumeration per
        section_02::verify_l7_canonicalize_idempotence)
      monotonicity (validates each CN-N rule rewrites within or below
        the partial order — no upward rewrites — preserving the
        monotone canonical form)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-02 lattice engine discharges L-7 via per-CN-rule idempotence enumeration + composition fixpoint argument
